  "id": "incomplete-spinal-cord-injury",
  "term": "incomplete spinal cord injury",
  "definition": "Incomplete spinal cord injury is a spinal cord injury that causes motor and sensory impairments without completely eliminating function. It can include reduced proprioceptive feedback, which may contribute to unsteady or insecure walking even in people who remain able to walk well.",
