      "reasons": [
        "The definition states that an incomplete spinal cord injury ‘causes motor and sensory impairments without completely eliminating function.’ The packet only states that incomplete spinal cord injury ‘leads to motor and sensory deficits’ and does not explicitly support the “without completely eliminating function” wording.",
        "The packet does support the related idea that impaired proprioception/internal afferent (feedback) can lead to an insecure gait (it mentions ‘impaired proprioception’ resulting in ‘an insecure gait’ and ‘limited internal afferent feedback’)."
